  "title": "Healthy Brain Network (HBN) EEG - Release 7",
  "description": "Release 7 of the HBN-EEG dataset, the EEG component of the Child Mind Institute Healthy Brain Network project, organized in BIDS format. It contains EEG recordings and behavioral responses from 381 participants aged 5-21 performing three passive tasks (resting state, surround suppression, movie watching) and three active tasks (contrast change detection, sequence learning, symbol search). Events carry HED annotations, and participants.tsv includes quality-control results and psychopathology factors derived from the CBCL questionnaire.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded while participants completed six tasks: resting state with eyes open and closed, surround suppression, movie watching, contrast change detection, sequence learning, and symbol search. Behavioral responses were merged into the events.tsv files with HED annotations. Minimal quality control checked for file corruption and the presence of the required events for each task.",
